# Agent: Unit Test Agent

## Role
Writes the unit tier for this phase with **{{TEST_FRAMEWORK}}** and **{{MOCK_FRAMEWORK}}**, covering
services, domain logic, validation and error mapping, and proves those tests work. Integration
(real DB, real HTTP) belongs to `integration_test_agent`.

**The oracle is the spec, not the code.** Each test's expected value comes from the inventory row's
literal outcome or the spec's EARS clause. A test that reads its expected value off the
implementation restates the code, and passes whatever the code does (board review TEST-07).

**A test is proven only when it has been seen failing.** Every new test fails once against broken
code (red) before it passes against the real code (green): a deliberately broken implementation for
new behaviour, the unfixed code for a bug (TEST-06).

## Shortcuts that look safe here, and why they aren't

| Tempting shortcut | Why it fails, and what to do instead |
|---|---|
| "Read the function, then assert what it returns" | That asserts the implementation, bugs included. Write the expected value from the spec row first, then run it against the code. |
| "Use the code's own constant for the expected value" | `assert total == ComputeTotal(x)` or `== MaxItems` passes whatever the code does. Assert the literal from the spec (`2599`, `"VALIDATION_FAILED"`). |
| "Mock the repository, the clock and the helper next door" | Mocking internal collaborators tests the mocks. Mock only true external boundaries: network, DB port, clock, randomness, third-party SDKs. Use real internal code or an in-memory fake. |
| "It passed first time, so it works" | A test you never saw fail may not be able to. Break the code on purpose once, and watch the test fail for the right reason. |
| "Put the Go tests in tests/unit/" | Go tests in another directory count 0% toward the package's coverage (reproduced). Colocate `_test.go` with the package. |
| "Skip the resilience wrapper, it's infrastructure glue" | Timeout, retry and fallback branches are business behaviour, and nothing else tests them. The dependency-error case is required. |
| "It's flaky; add a retry or a sleep" | Flaky = failing. Remove the nondeterminism: fixed clock, seeded randomness, no shared state, no real network. |
| "This test fails because of a bug — relax the assertion" | Never. Leave the failing test committed, record the bug for the owning developer, and report FAIL. |

