## Evidence (what the gate reads — skills/testing/test-results-sidecar.md)

```bash
P="agent_state/phases/{{PHASE}}"; mkdir -p "$P/junit" "$P/reports"
git add <your test files> && git commit -m "phase {{PHASE}}: unit tests (TC-…)"      # 1. commit first: evidence binds to the code commit
CMD="$(jq -r '.commands["test:unit"]' agent_state/config/verify-commands.json)"     # 2. the table's command, nothing else
[ -n "$CMD" ] && [ "$CMD" != null ] || { echo "BLOCKED: no test:unit command in verify-commands.json"; exit 1; }
PHASE={{PHASE}} bash -c "$CMD" > "$P/junit/unit.log" 2>&1; RC=$?                     # no pipe: keep the real exit code
python3 .claude/hooks/junit-to-sidecar.py --tier unit --command "$CMD" --exit-code $RC \
  --priorities "$P/tc_priorities.json" --out "$P/reports/unit_tests.json" "$P/junit/unit.xml"   # 3. runner output → sidecar
```

- The JUnit path is the one the command writes: under `agent_state/phases/{{PHASE}}/junit/`. A report
  written inside the source tree makes the code "dirty", and the gate rejects the evidence.
- **No retries to green.** Don't add a rerun flag (`gotestsum --rerun-fails`, `jest --retry`) to get
  green. A pass on retry counts as `flaky`, and flaky > 0 fails the gate.
- **Quarantine** only with an issue link and an expiry of at most 14 days, in the sidecar's
  `quarantined[]`. Never with a silent skip.
- Go runs with `-count=1` (no cache), and with `-race` where cgo allows. The table's command should
  already say so. If it doesn't, report the missing flag rather than working around it.
- `unit_tests.md` explains the sidecar. It isn't evidence. `test_runner` re-runs the tier in Wave 3v and
  refreshes `unit_tests.json` from its own run.

