## Test File Layout

| Stack | Where unit tests go | Coverage per package |
|---|---|---|
| Go | beside the code: `internal/order/total_test.go` (`package order`, or `package order_test` for black-box) | `go test -count=1 -cover ./...` prints `coverage: N%` per package; or `-coverprofile` + `go tool cover -func` |
| TypeScript / JS | beside the module: `src/order/total.test.ts` (Vitest/Jest default include is `*.test.*` / `*.spec.*` — `total_test.ts` never runs) | `coverage/coverage-summary.json` (reporter `json-summary`) |
| Python | `tests/unit/test_<module>.py` | `pytest --cov=<pkg> --cov-report=term-missing` per module |
| Java / Kotlin | `src/test/java/<same package>/<Class>Test.java` | JaCoCo per package |
| Rust | `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` in the same file | `cargo llvm-cov --summary-only` |

Shared test helpers go in the package's own test files, or a small `internal/testutil` / `test/fixtures` module.

